rtion  that a very gun adept that truly know  how to handle so it would just be a very  small group of people that are very gun  adept I've listened to the first grade  teachers that don't want to be pistol  packin first grade teachers I've  listened to law enforcement who have  said they don't want to have to train  teachers as law enforcement agencies  which takes about six months so I just  suggest we need a little less tweeting  here a little more listening damn what  about this I mean there's a gaining  traction or taking away right I think  it's gonna be a state-by-state thing  there are a number of Governors I was  covering the governor's all weekend and  in talking to them there are a number of  Governors in both parties who are  uncomfortable with this idea but we  should point out some of them I'm  already doing it and we talked with with  Governor Abbott in Texas about what they  have done and I think there's they said  almost a fifth of the schools there have  people who are armed and this is  something that in part will have to do  with the culture of each of those states  the culture of the use of guns and how  comfortable people are with it but there  are a number of governors who say  including Republican governors adding  adding guns to this environment is not  what they want to see in schools but  we'll see how this debate goes forward  state-by-state yeah speaking of culture  I want to play one more soundbite this  is from Kentucky's governor  we have to talk about the culture in  this society and when we mock and  ridicule the very foundational  principles that this nation was built  upon where you treat people the way  you'd want to be treated where you  respect human life where you respect the  dignity of women and of children and a  people who we have been creasing ly  degraded in our society this culture of  death is becoming pervasive hard to  legislate something like that but he was  talking about using the bullet pulp  bully pulpits in all